🎯 REMEMBER THE CORE PURPOSE

The Complete RAG → LLM → Code Generation → Execution Workflow

User Query ("What genes does TP53 regulate?")
    ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ RAG Retrieval (parallel search)                │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Embedding1: title + @description               │
│ Embedding2: @section User Queries             │
│ → Retrieve + Union → Return matches            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LLM Function Selection                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Input: title + @description from candidates    │
│ LLM decides: "gpdb_find_targets is best match"│
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LLM Code Generation                            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Input: title + @param + usage + @examples     │
│ Note: usage auto-generated from function def  │
│ LLM writes: result <- gpdb_find_targets(...)  │
│ → Execute in container                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    ↓
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LLM Next Step (Continuous Execution)          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Input: @return + "What You Can Do Next"       │
│ LLM sees: "Enrich with gpdb_enrich()..."      │
│ LLM writes next code → Continuous workflow    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Critical Documentation Elements for This Workflow

Element
Purpose
Why Critical
@title + @description
LLM function selection
Embedded as embedding1, must distinguish functions
@section User Queries
RAG retrieval
Embedded as embedding2, natural language entry
@param + @examples
Code generation
Must be verified/executable for accurate code
@return + "What You Can Do Next"
Continuous execution
LLM knows how to chain analysis steps
@references
Citation/reproducibility
For scientific reporting

Cursor AI's Role
- Read this .cursorrules file
- Understand the complete RAG → LLM workflow
- Optimize documentation to enable this workflow
  
Five Core Principles
1. Code-Logic-First: Read code BEFORE writing (avoid hallucination)
2. Evidence-Based: Use REAL test results (examples must work)
3. Database-Backed: Document database scope and confidence levels
4. English Only: ALL documentation in English
5. Executable: Ask user when stuck, don't guess
  
核心原则：先理解代码逻辑，再写文档。基于真实测试结果，不基于想象。遇到困难就问用户。


